WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.607
Now consider a more dangerous case.

00:00:02.607 --> 00:00:07.517
Suppose one patient has three admissions and four lab results.

00:00:07.517 --> 00:00:14.704
If we join admissions to lab results only by patient, we can create twelve combined rows.

00:00:15.394 --> 00:00:21.676
If we then count admissions or sum another measure, the results may look reasonable but be wrong because the join

00:00:21.676 --> 00:00:29.145
multiplied the facts first. This is why you should check cardinality before reshaping joined data.
